%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%
%% Automatic cataloging: settlement IS registration (DECISIONS D-004, D-022).
%% Proven live: EVIDENCE S3-3 (listing created), S3-4 (hostile writes soft-dropped).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant B as Stock buyer
  participant S as Seller<br/>(declareDiscoveryExtension<br/>in route config — F-074)
  participant W as walras /settle
  participant I as bazaar indexer
  participant D as SQLite catalog

  B->>S: GET /resource
  S-->>B: 402 — resource block carries the bazaar extension
  B->>S: paid retry — the CLIENT echoes the extension<br/>into PaymentPayload (F-032 — no echo, no listing)
  S->>W: POST /settle
  Note over W: settlement completes on-chain first —<br/>the payment path never waits on indexing (D-015)
  W->>I: indexSettledPayment(payload, requirements)
  Note over I: protocol invariants + client schema +<br/>soft-drop metadata rules + routeTemplate<br/>percent-decode-before-traversal-checks<br/>(F-030, F-031, F-072)
  alt info valid — key unowned or owned by this payTo
    I->>D: upsert keyed (resource, type, toolName),<br/>owned by first settled payTo (F-029, D-024)
    W-->>S: EXTENSION-RESPONSES bazaar.status success
  else client-attributable defect
    I-->>W: rejected + machine code (bazaar_*)
    W-->>S: EXTENSION-RESPONSES bazaar.status rejected,<br/>rejectedReason + code (D-014)
  else internal indexer fault
    I-->>W: error (never thrown into the response path)
    W-->>S: header omitted — a walras fault is not<br/>blamed on the client (D-025)
  end
  Note over W,S: the SettleResponse body is identical in all three branches
